-- DICT-SEMANTICS §3 (`inst`, matching set) / §4.2 (obligation deferral):
-- an inferred binding whose residual predicate has a MIXED argument vector --
-- one STRUCTURED argument (`Wrap α`) and one open tyvar -- must not be allowed
-- to reach `main` unchecked when NOTHING in the program can ever satisfy it.
--
-- REGRESSION GUARD FOR #1578 (mixed vector, no matching impl, silent), S0,
-- fixed by sprint/entailment-verdict. Written because the fix DELETED the
-- self-draining pin `test/must_fail_fixtures/1578-mixed-vector-no-matching-
-- impl-silent/` per [G-PIN-DRAIN] and left the S0 with no guard at all: a pin
-- asserts a bug STILL REPRODUCES, so draining one removes the guard unless a
-- positive row replaces it. This is that row.
--
-- SPEC ANSWER (hand-derived from §3, NOT captured). `h x y = conv (Wrap x) y`
-- raises the goal `Conv (Wrap α) β`. §3's matching set is ONE φ against the
-- WHOLE vector: φ(`Conv Int Bool`) would need `Wrap α = Int`, and `Wrap` is a
-- declared tycon that is not `Int`, so no φ exists. The set is EMPTY on the
-- structured argument alone -- no instantiation of β can rescue it -- and the
-- program declares no other `Conv` impl, so `main`'s ground goal
-- `Conv (Wrap Int) Bool` is likewise unsatisfiable. THE PROGRAM IS REJECTED,
-- T-NO-IMPL, on check, run AND build.
--
-- MEASURED AT THE PRE-SPRINT ARM `264eb95d` (this tree, cold-built): the whole
-- vector was checked on argument 0 only or not at all -- `check` exit 0 with an
-- empty `--json` diagnostics list, `run` exit 0 PRINTING `int-bool` (the body of
-- an impl the goal matches on NEITHER argument), and only `build` died, at the
-- emitter, `no impl of method 'conv' for type 'Wrap'`. Silent wrongness on two
-- of three verbs.
--
-- ⚠️ THIS ROW PINS THE VERDICT AND THE DIAGNOSTIC CODE, DELIBERATELY NOT THE
-- LOCATION, and that is load-bearing rather than lazy. On this binary the
-- rejection lands at `h`'s DEFINITION line, which is the same site #1939 (OPEN
-- regression, this sprint's own) falsely rejects a LEGAL binding at. #1939's
-- fix will move where a structured-argument obligation is adjudicated; it must
-- not be able to green this program, because `main` forces the ground goal
-- `Conv (Wrap Int) Bool` and that goal is unsatisfiable wherever it is checked.
-- A row that pinned that location would have enshrined #1939's behaviour as
-- correct.
data Wrap a = Wrap a

interface Conv a b where
  conv : a -> b -> String

impl Conv Int Bool where
  conv _ _ = "int-bool"

h x y = conv (Wrap x) y

main = println (h 5 True)
